  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—namely, the probabilities of a favorable (non-zero) outcome and the assumption that outcome differences are negligible—aligns with what the individual considered. The individual noted that Lottery B 'almost guarantees a win,' which directly reflects attention to the high probability of a positive outcome. Furthermore, the justification ('therefore the choice') is based solely on this high probability, consistent with the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with the higher chance of a favorable outcome when outcome differences are treated as negligible. There is no indication of consideration of expected value, risk aversion, or outcome magnitude comparisons, which supports the alignment with the stated reason. The verbal report strongly reflects the core logic of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

